{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: Production durable hosted coding runtime. Implementation work package 3 of the reviewed connected-story design (planning b5f1fb3f, exact Draft2 evidence209a5ec9, approvalfc77cf82 and adopted direction0f358e52). Source baseline e6e6782 and the active acts/MCP a199 composition are context, not approval; reconcile current reviewed main, relevant existing requests and ecbc722a runner changes before editing.\n\nScope and decisions:\nBuild the production Agent package and isolated coding controller, reusing pi-durable SQLite conversation/outbox patterns and the existing client/Git owners. The pi spike's controlled Workspace double and caller-driven run are not real filesystem/process durability or an autonomous production scheduler. One Agent Durable Object owns conversation, durable inputs, exact signed act outbox, operation ledger and checkpoint manifests. Map the environment to room/lane/holder/lease generation/workspace epoch; persist replacement instance IDs. Keep Room/agent signing keys, operator/model credentials and canonical write tokens outside repository execution.\nImplement real read/edit/command/dependency/Git preparation tools using the reviewed recovery strategy. Acknowledge only persisted work and return stored completed command receipts. Reconcile unfinished commands and fork pushes before further mutating tools; never have the model reconstruct missing edits or conclude unknown effects absent. Persist original declared binding in an act outbox; a new meaning requires a new action. Autonomous alarms, bounded scheduling, attention delivery, lease renew/release, current authority checks, budgets and checkpoint retention must work without browser heartbeats. Existing Room/Git owners still mint/revoke fork tokens, settle uncertain operations and own canonical publication.\nPause stops new tools, finishes/reconciles the current tool, checkpoints and suspends idle compute with visible lease expiry. Browser disconnect continues authorized active work. A proposal awaiting review is not terminal landing. Cancel is durable and pending while effects or publication are unsettled. Lease/holder changes fence old writes immediately; fresh holders get fresh environments and private checkpoint transfer needs explicit authorization. Human-key revocation and agent-key/grant revocation have the distinct effects in the contract. Owned payload expiry/cleanup keeps Room history and unresolved operation tombstones.\nApply the reconciled design decisions, not Draft1 wording: existing sessions are read-only; controls use signed resource/action-bound current owner/admin requests. Initially one new agent member and one DO/conversation/lane per task; no in-place owner reassignment. Last-active-owner-key revocation or owner removal stops new tools/broker writes/renewals; another active owner device keeps independent-agent work alive. Admins retain private export/settlement, and lost-key recovery restores only an active member, never a removed handle. Optional delegated agent mode is not required in initial runtime delivery; its key-bound grantor rules and conditional acceptance remain specified. Render repository/command output inert in the key-owning origin and expose only minimal activity to other Room readers.\nSaved root includes ignored/generated/dependency project files and self-contained Git storage; external Git alternates/directories are dissociated into owned storage or refused, symlinks are not followed outside, special files fail saves explicitly, and out-of-root persistent work is unsupported initially. Quiesce detached child writers. Persist/verify all payload and object closure before manifest; atomically commit receipt/current checkpoint under current epoch/instance/base, then ack. Preserve the last good checkpoint on limits/save failure, separating observed exit from durable result. Old callbacks cannot replace a new current receipt/pointer/commit. A new command attempt has a distinct linked ID and never closes the old unknown duty. Pin bytes/objects needed by outstanding effects; legally expire checkpoint/export roots in a durable purge transaction and return explicit expired/unknown on old-ID retries after permitted deletion.\nOwn the existing client settlement gap in packages/client/src/connect.ts and RPC wire helpers: add service-binding submission of retained signed envelopes without connection, fresh read session or new signature. Existing HTTPS resubmit is an available route. Recover admitted receipts after revocation while refusing new acts, grants and tool dispatch.\nPrivate-read contract decision carried from independent revised-design review: initial raw owner/admin resources require a direct device read session, whose direct-key provenance and current role/resource are verified by the trusted Room boundary. authenticateRead returning an owner/admin member handle is insufficient. Deny delegation-issued read sessions raw resources by default; any separately scoped private-read capability is later explicit contract work. Sessions stay read-only, and controls remain separately signed.\n\nDependencies and order:\nRequired relevant reviewed decisions/deliveries: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b538c5eace50a1de82a8bdf8a8f19764548af15e, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6cdaf20fa260d6d6c6b30e83f585883a51b964f4. Reviewed authority/lifecycle contract; reviewed real recovery spike and resolved blocking findings; existing acts/client/fork/credential work. Reconcile production pi scheduler/attention work already specified rather than replacing its obligations. Highest implementation priority remains test-overhead ecbc722a, followed by acts and builder-identified Jam blockers; this request adds no first-Jam readiness gate. Report source/design discrepancies before weakening scope.\n\nAcceptance outcome:\nA real repository task edits files, runs a useful command, survives abrupt host/controller loss and resumes with exact saved state and operation receipts. The runtime runs and renews as authorized after the initiating browser disconnects, delivers attention once, accepts steering durably at a tool boundary, pauses/cancels visibly, fences stale authority and retains uncertain work. Prepare/push one exact head and record a normal proposal; distinct human review and qualified checks lead through existing landing/publication. No repository command gains Room/operator/main credentials. Include one detached writer, stale save callback and failed save retaining the prior good checkpoint. A second authorized command attempt leaves the first unknown duty open; purge preserves required pins and a legally deleted result returns expired rather than dispatching anew. Recover an admitted act's receipt after its signing key is revoked, without reacquiring a read session or making a new signed act.\n\nValidation:\nDefine package-local typecheck and runtime/probe scripts for the new Agent package and name them in the promise. Existing affected client runners are npm run test:node and test:workerd --workspace @generalbusiness/artroom-client; Room's corresponding commands cover real auth/lease admission. Use focused files, real DO recovery and the reviewed provider probe. Run one final retained invariant gate at delivered head, not repeated root builds per interruption point.\n\nDelivery: use an isolated request branch/worktree, record promise and exact source/probe evidence, publish every changed path at the exact delivered head, and obtain independent normal review before integration. Source code/protocol amendments are not authorized by the evidence-only design verdict alone. No numerical test inventory/per-guard sweep, no new first-Jam readiness gate. If a provider/storage/authority mechanism cannot meet the stated story, report a design discrepancy rather than silently reducing scope.","body":{"conditions":"A real repository task edits files, runs a useful command, survives abrupt host/controller loss and resumes with exact saved state and operation receipts. The runtime runs and renews as authorized after the initiating browser disconnects, delivers attention once, accepts steering durably at a tool boundary, pauses/cancels visibly, fences stale authority and retains uncertain work. Prepare/push one exact head and record a normal proposal; distinct human review and qualified checks lead through existing landing/publication. No repository command gains Room/operator/main credentials. Include one detached writer, stale save callback and failed save retaining the prior good checkpoint. A second authorized command attempt leaves the first unknown duty open; purge preserves required pins and a legally deleted result returns expired rather than dispatching anew. Recover an admitted act's receipt after its signing key is revoked, without reacquiring a read session or making a new signed act. Required relevant reviewed decisions/deliveries: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b538c5eace50a1de82a8bdf8a8f19764548af15e, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6cdaf20fa260d6d6c6b30e83f585883a51b964f4. Relevant contract decisions and exact implementation evidence independently reviewed; source artifacts integrated through normal landing. Preserve named lifecycle/authority/durability rules and existing owed work. Define package-local typecheck and runtime/probe scripts for the new Agent package and name them in the promise. Existing affected client runners are npm run test:node and test:workerd --workspace @generalbusiness/artroom-client; Room's corresponding commands cover real auth/lease admission. Use focused files, real DO recovery and the reviewed provider probe. Run one final retained invariant gate at delivered head, not repeated root builds per interruption point.","dependencies":"Required relevant reviewed decisions/deliveries: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b538c5eace50a1de82a8bdf8a8f19764548af15e, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6cdaf20fa260d6d6c6b30e83f585883a51b964f4. Reviewed authority/lifecycle contract; reviewed real recovery spike and resolved blocking findings; existing acts/client/fork/credential work. Reconcile production pi scheduler/attention work already specified rather than replacing its obligations. Highest implementation priority remains test-overhead ecbc722a, followed by acts and builder-identified Jam blockers; this request adds no first-Jam readiness gate. Report source/design discrepancies before weakening scope.","priority":"After highest-priority test-overhead ecbc722a; preserve acts/Jam-blocker/Jam-and-docs order. No new first-Jam gate.","target_head":"e6e6782830e0ca8a68f0d11c4d4ece5e4e98c967","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}